    "theoryUz": "### Transfer learning va fine-tuning farqi\n\n**1. Konseptual Asos va Muammo (Core Problem & Concept):**\n“Transfer learning va fine-tuning farqi” — Transformerlar va Zamonaviy NLP yo'nalishining asosiy qismlaridan biridir.\nUshbu mavzuda o'rganiladigan asosiy terminlar: Self-Attention, Scaled Dot-Product, Multi-Head Attention, Positional Encoding, BERT, GPT, Masked LM.\n«Transfer learning va fine-tuning farqi» mavzusining nima ekanini, qayerda va nima uchun ishlatilishini mustaqil tushuntira olish.\n\n**2. Ishlash Mexanizmi va Matematik Mantiq (Under the Hood):**\nTransformer vositalari yordamida parametrlar va matritsalar qat'iy mantiqiy ketma-ketlikda transformatsiya qilinadi. Kiruvchi ma'lumotlar o'lchami tekshiriladi, xatoliklar (chegaraviy shartlar) filtrlangan holda optimal natija hosil qilinadi.\n\n**3. Ishlab chiqarish Qoidalari (Production Best Practices):**\nProduction quvurlarida ushbu usul ma'lumotlar oqimining barqarorligi, xotira tejamkorligi va modelning barqaror bashorat berishini kafolatlaydi.",
    "visualFlow": [
      {
        "step": 1,
        "label": "Q, K, V Proyeksiyalari",
        "detail": "Har bir token uchun Query, Key va Value vektorlari"
      },
      {
        "step": 2,
        "label": "E'tibor Ballari (QK^T)",
        "detail": "Barcha so'zlarning bir-biriga bog'liqlik matritsasi"
      },
      {
        "step": 3,
        "label": "Masshtablash va Softmax",
        "detail": "sqrt(d_k) ga bo'lib ehtimolliklar matritsasini olish"
      },
      {
        "step": 4,
        "label": "Kontekstli Chiqish",
        "detail": "Value vektorlarini e'tibor vaznlari bilan jamlash"
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": "ex-mlds-29-15-1",
        "titleUz": "1-misol: Transfer learning va fine-tuning farqi — Scaled Dot-Product Attention Formulasi",
        "explanationUz": "Formula: $\\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\text{softmax}\\left(\\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right) V$.",
        "code": "import numpy as np\n\ndef scaled_dot_product_attention(Q: np.ndarray, K: np.ndarray, V: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    d_k = Q.shape[-1]\n    scores = np.dot(Q, K.T) / np.sqrt(d_k)\n    # Softmax\n    exp_scores = np.exp(scores - np.max(scores, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    attention_weights = exp_scores / np.sum(exp_scores, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    output = np.dot(attention_weights, V)\n    return np.round(output, 3)\n\n# 2 ta token, o'lcham d_k = 2\nQ = np.array([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]])\nK = np.array([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]])\nV = np.array([[10.0, 20.0], [30.0, 40.0]])\nprint(\"Attention chiqishi:\\n\", scaled_dot_product_attention(Q, K, V))",
        "expectedOutput": "Attention chiqishi:\n [[15.826 25.826]\n [24.174 34.174]]"
      },
      {
        "id": "ex-mlds-29-15-2",
        "titleUz": "2-misol: Transfer learning va fine-tuning farqi — Sinusoidal Positional Encoding Simulyatsiyasi",
        "explanationUz": "Transformer so'zlar tartibini bilmagani sababli joylashuv pozitsiyasini kiritish talab etiladi.",
        "code": "import math\n\ndef get_positional_encoding(pos: int, d_model: int = 4) -> list[float]:\n    pe = []\n    for i in range(0, d_model, 2):\n        pe.append(round(math.sin(pos / (10000 ** (i / d_model))), 3))\n        pe.append(round(math.cos(pos / (10000 ** (i / d_model))), 3))\n    return pe\n\nprint(\"0-pozitsiya kodi:\", get_positional_encoding(0))\nprint(\"1-pozitsiya kodi:\", get_positional_encoding(1))",
        "expectedOutput": "0-pozitsiya kodi: [0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0]\n1-pozitsiya kodi: [0.841, 0.54, 0.01, 1.0]"
      }
    ],
